                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "IUxx5",
                      "name": "Notes",
                      "fill": "#1A1400",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": 640,
                      "content": "A grid of monospace characters, about 200 by 60, redrawn every frame. Each cell picks a character and ink strength from drifting noise, two overlapping sine ripples, and a 3D ring traced per cell and lit from the upper left; denser characters read brighter.\n\nMotion: the ring turns once a minute, the noise drifts slower, and about one cell in a thousand blinks an amber cursor.\n\nChecking: the ring spins 2.6× faster and amber rings leave the button every 1.25 s.\nRefused: the grid fills solid with @ and % in half a second, crumbles top-down into × marks, goes blank, and returns after about 5 s.\n\nPalette: paper #11100E, ink #DCD5C3, accent #E5A00D (Plex amber).\nFont: IBM Plex Mono.\nCost: 11–14 ms a frame at retina density, about 60 fps; 7 ms at half resolution (MAX_DPR = 1).\nNext: try a light-paper version, dark ink on #ECE7D8.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
