                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "KO5Tx",
                      "name": "Notes",
                      "fill": "#1A1A1A",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": 640,
                      "content": "The screen is a grid of monospace characters cut into 6×3-cell blocks, the pieces of a torrent, grouped into up to 16 rectangles that stand for files. Each file loops: pieces land in a shuffled, clumped order with a short bright flash, the file holds complete, then a thin bar plays it left to right and the cells behind it thin back to dots.\n\nA file cycle takes 35–53 s; the bar crosses a file in about 10 s.\n\nChecking: the clock runs 2.2× faster and fresh pieces pile up beside the button. Refused: arrivals stop and pieces drop from the edges inward, marked ×. Success: a wave from the button completes every piece in about 1.6 s, lime on black, then holds.\n\nPaper #0C0D0A. Ink #34352D, #7D7B6D, #D8D4C4, #F6F3E8. Lime #C6F135, dim lime #5F7A16 on #000000. Font: Berkeley Mono.\n\nCost: 1.7 ms per frame at 1x, 4.2 ms at retina, 10 ms during the success wave. No half-resolution trick needed.\n\nNext: drive the piece arrivals from real rTorrent progress.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                      "fontSize": 16,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
