                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": 640,
                      "content": "How it works: a monospace grid (about 205 × 58 cells) where six horizontal bands of glyph density scroll left to right. Each band's thickness comes from 1D noise, so it reads like a bandwidth graph. A soft vertical buffer front sits at 70% width: behind it the bands are dense ink, at it they flicker as hex digits, ahead of it they are faint dots.\n\nMotion: bands flow at 4–7 cells a second. Faint dash lines between bands drift the other way at about 3 (upload). The front sways slowly.\n\nChecking: the front stops and the strip behind it swells to solid. Refused: static across the grid, then one flat line. Success: the front crosses the screen in 0.9 s, everything turns #C6F135 on #000000, then holds.\n\nPalette: paper #0E0F0D, ink #D8DBCE / #80847A / #3D4039. Font: Berkeley Mono.\nCost: 2.6 ms a frame at 1×, 5.6 ms at 2× (1440 × 900). Next: drive flow speed from the real download rate.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.5,
                      "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                      "fontSize": 18,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
