                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "Hkej0",
                      "name": "Notes",
                      "width": 620,
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "UMSyK",
                          "name": "Notes heading",
                          "fill": "#1A1400",
                          "content": "Notes",
                          "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                          "fontSize": 20,
                          "fontWeight": "700"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "bBR40",
                          "name": "Notes body",
                          "fill": "#2A2A2A",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Five globes, each drawn pixel by pixel: the code finds the point on the sphere behind every pixel, turns it by the globe's spin and feeds it to that globe's formula (crossing ring waves, dots sized by latitude, contour lines, flipping Truchet tiles, bent bands). The result is lit from one side and dithered to six inks, over the faint particle current from concept 2.\n\nGlobes drift a few percent of the screen over 70–120 s and turn once every 42–86 s.\n\nChecking: formulas run 5x faster and the light circles the globes every 4 s. Refused: two inks only, globes drift off screen. Success: light swings to the front, lit sides go #C6F135, the near globe swells 1.5x over 2 s, then holds.\n\nInks: #0D1122 ground, #1A2341, #34446B, #6A7EA6, #AEBCD8, #EEF1F7.\nFont: Berkeley Mono.\nCost: 10–13 ms per frame at half resolution.\nNext: move the formulas to a WebGL shader and render at full resolution.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.5,
                          "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                          "fontSize": 16,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T02yX",
          "name": "Round 4 title",
          "fill": "#1A1400",
          "content": "ROUND 4 — WINNER: Concept 2d, the planet (Alec, 11 Oct 2026)",
          "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
          "fontSize": 36,
          "fontWeight": "800"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "g71qX",
          "name": "Lanes round 4",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": 40,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "rEE91",
              "name": "Lane 2d winner",
              "width": 1680,
              "fill": "#FFFFFF",
              "stroke": "#1A1400",
              "strokeWidth": 3,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 24,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "z6JqH",
                  "name": "Lane label",
                  "fill": "#1A1400",
                  "content": "Concept 2d — Planet (winner)",
                  "fontFamily": "Schibsted Grotesk",
                  "fontSize": 32,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "ZYuQv",
                  "name": "Idle grid",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 24,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "OhnKj",
                      "name": "Idle row 1",
                      "gap": 24,
